        CLERK’S CORNEREarly Voting begins on October 16th for the 2024 General Election.The Clerk’s office will be ready for you during the hours of 9am-3pm, Monday through Friday, October 16th -November 4th. (Nov. 4th until 4pm) **Please remember to bring your current government issued ID with you. ** Do you need a mail ballot?The deadline for mail ballot applications is on October 15th at 4pm.Applications can be found online through the Secretary of State’s website  vote.ri.govOr the Clerk’s Office at the Town Hall  Questions? Please call 401-466-3201.General Election Election DatesThe General Election will be Tuesday, November 5, 2024 at the Town Hall, Old Town Road. In order to participate, you must be registered to vote in New Shoreham on or before Sunday, October 6, 2024. You may register at the Town Clerk’s Office, Town Hall, Old Town Road, Block Island during regular business hours Monday through Friday 9:00 to 3:00. On Friday, October 4, 2024  you may use the elections drop-box outside of Town Hall (registration forms will be available).Register to VoteVoters must register 30 days before an election. You must be registered to vote from your actual place of residence. You may register in person at Town Hall, at the DMV, online(vote.ri.gov) or by mail:The New Shoreham Board of CanvassersP.O. Box 220Block Island, RI 02807 For additional information, including a MAIL BALLOT APPLICATION, visit vote.ri.gov
    


